## Diagrams

**System diagram** — what talks to what. The visitor's hand and movement feed two inputs
(ultrasonic sensor, webcam); the Arduino and the p5.js sketch exchange messages over USB; the
outputs are the gear train that moves the real leaf, and the screen.

![System diagram](../../assets/images/thelastleaf/system_diagram.png)

My first hand sketch of the system mixed the parts and the states in one picture, which is why I
split it into a system diagram and a state diagram.

![First system sketch by hand](../../assets/images/thelastleaf/system_sketch_by_hand.jpg)

**State diagram** — what happens over time: IDLE → DROP → WAIT → PAINT → RETURN, with what the
physical piece and the screen each do in every state, and the trigger for each step.

![State diagram](../../assets/images/thelastleaf/state_diagram.png)

**Circuit diagram** — servo on D9, HC-SR04 on D7/D6, 100 µF capacitor across the 5 V rail.

![Circuit diagram](../../assets/images/thelastleaf/circuit_diagram.png)

